## Source Code

File: `src/main.cpp`

```cpp
#include <Arduino.h>

#define LED_PIN 23
#define BUTTON_PIN 18

void setup() {
    pinMode(LED_PIN, OUTPUT);
    pinMode(BUTTON_PIN, INPUT_PULLUP);
}

void loop() {
    if (digitalRead(BUTTON_PIN) == LOW) {
        digitalWrite(LED_PIN, HIGH);
    }
    else {
        digitalWrite(LED_PIN, LOW);
    }
}
```

---

## Working Principle

1. The ESP32 is powered through a USB connection.
2. GPIO 23 is configured as an OUTPUT to control the LED.
3. GPIO 18 is configured as `INPUT_PULLUP` to detect the push button.
4. When the button is released, the internal pull-up resistor keeps GPIO 18 HIGH.
5. Pressing the button connects GPIO 18 to GND, making the input LOW.
6. The ESP32 detects the LOW signal and sets GPIO 23 HIGH, turning the LED ON.
7. Releasing the button returns GPIO 18 to HIGH, turning the LED OFF.

### Logic Table

| Button State | GPIO 18 | LED |
|---|---|---|
| Released | HIGH (1) | OFF |
| Pressed | LOW (0) | ON |

